{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\uc1\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}{\f1 Courier New;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;}{\stylesheet{\s0\f0\fs22 Normal;}{\s1\sbasedon0\keepn\fs38 Title;}{\s2\sbasedon0\keepn\outlinelevel0\fs29 Heading 1;}{\s3\sbasedon0\keepn\outlinelevel1\fs24 Heading 2;}}\paperw11906\paperh16838\margl1134\margr1134\margt1134\margb1134\widowctrl\f0\fs22\cf1{\footer\pard\qc\f0\fs18 Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}}\pard\s1\keepn\sb0\sa240\b\fs38 Dana Motors receipts and party accounts frontend testing guide\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 This guide explains the complete receipts and party-account flow for issue 77 and gives frontend acceptance steps with expected balances. Start with a disposable test environment and follow the scenarios in order.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 How the flow works\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 A job bill creates a debit owed by the customer. A payment receipt creates credit; any unallocated remainder stays available as an advance. Credit notes and opening credits add to that same available credit. Debit notes and opening debits add outstanding debt. An adjustment matches equal debit and credit amounts, reducing both without changing the party net. Reports reconstruct balances at the chosen date. Letters save a snapshot of that dated net and its documents.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Start the local test application\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Use the repository's configured test environment, with dependencies already installed. In a terminal at server, run npm run db:prepare to apply migrations and generate Prisma, then npm run dev. In a second terminal at client, run npm run dev. The default browser address is http://localhost:3000 and the backend default is http://localhost:8000. Use your approved test staff accounts; this guide does not create or disclose passwords. Restart the backend and sign in again after migrations/permission changes.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Prerequisites\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Use a migrated test database and staff accounts for Admin, Accountant/BillingOfficer, and a user without receipt:adjust. Refresh sessions after permission changes. Select the intended branch in the header. Create a test customer and unposted invoices/receipts. Keep a second branch/customer for access tests. Do not run testing against production financial records.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Prepare a bill and receipt through the frontend\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. Create or choose a test customer and vehicle in the selected branch. Have a job card ready for billing with its latest estimate approved and a service advisor assigned. Complete the existing workshop job flow first; a delivered job requires its approved credit exception.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Open Finance \u8594? Invoices \u8594? New invoice. Choose the billable job card and advisor, review the server-calculated lines, discounts, VAT and total, then create the job bill. Record its number, total, outstanding and due date. A job cannot have two active bills.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. Open Finance \u8594? Receipts \u8594? Payment receipt. Choose the same customer, receiving mode/bank, amount and narration. Leave allocation empty for an advance, or choose invoice allocation amounts within the current outstanding. Save and record the receipt number and remaining advance.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. The numeric examples below assume test invoices with totals exactly 10,000 or 5,000. Have those fixtures prepared, or substitute your actual server-calculated totals and recompute expected balances. A line price of 10,000 before VAT is not an invoice total of 10,000. Do not manually overwrite invoice amounts to match an example.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Phase 2 advances openings and adjustments\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. Open Customer \u8594? Account. Record an opening \b credit of NGN 2,000\b0  with a date before the planned adjustment and a narration. Expect available credit 2,000. Only Admin/SuperAdmin with the opening permission sees the action.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Open Finance \u8594? Payment Receipt, choose the customer, receive \b NGN 5,000\b0  without allocating it. Expect a receipt advance of 5,000 and combined available credit \b 7,000\b0  on the Account tab and portal.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. Create an unposted invoice with outstanding \b NGN 10,000\b0 . Open its receipt capture and choose \b Use existing advances / credits\b0 . The adjustment workspace should preselect the customer.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. Select that invoice as Debit and the advance receipt as Credit. Enter \b 3,000\b0  on both sides. Expect difference 0 and enabled Save. Save once. Invoice outstanding becomes \b 7,000\b0 , receipt available becomes \b 2,000\b0 , combined credit becomes \b 4,000\b0 . Net outstanding stays \b 3,000\b0  because adjustment moves equal debit and credit amounts.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 5. Enter unequal amounts, more than an available document balance, zero, a negative amount, or three decimal places. Expect inline validation and disabled Save. Changing pages preserves selected amounts and totals. Refresh balances clears the selection.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 6. Enable FIFO. Expect oldest date/number first and editable amounts. With the preceding fixture, it should match remaining credit \b 4,000\b0  against the invoice. Save; invoice outstanding becomes \b 3,000\b0 , credits become \b 0\b0 . No new cash receipt or Tally adjustment journal is created.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 7. As Admin, reverse the FIFO batch from Recent adjustments with a reason. Expect invoice outstanding \b 7,000\b0 , combined credit \b 4,000\b0 , status Reversed and saved reason. A second reversal is rejected. Accountant/BillingOfficer can adjust but cannot reverse or record openings.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 8. Try changing the original receipt amount or cancelling it while the manual batch is active. Expect a message requiring reversal first. Narration-only editing should preserve balances. Reverse the manual batch, then cancellation may proceed if the receipt is unposted.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 9. Export/post an involved test invoice or receipt using the existing Tally flow. Try reversal; expect rejection with no balance change. Use a separate test fixture/company backup for Tally.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 10. Record an opening \b debit\b0  with date/narration. Expect it in Debits and in Account outstanding; it may be matched against a receipt or opening credit. It must never appear in Tally posting batches.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 11. As an assigned branch user, search and direct navigation must not expose a foreign branch party or documents. Admin can select another branch. A party with no matching documents shows an empty state.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 12. Create a credit application for an invoice, approve it in the customer portal, and verify invoice outstanding plus available credit decrease by the approved amount. Approval uses the same canonical allocation records; repeated approval creates no second adjustment. Decline changes no balance.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Evidence to capture: before/after Account totals, invoice outstanding, debit/credit grids, FIFO amounts, reversal reason/status, permission/access errors, and Tally reversal rejection. Browser screenshots and executed manual results will be recorded separately from automated test evidence.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Accountant access check: the customer directory and customer detail/document/history reads must stay within the assigned branch. An Accountant without a branch cannot read these screens. Global duplicate lookup is unavailable to Accountant. Admin can open another branch\u8217?s customer Account tab.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Phase 3 party reports and flow\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. Refresh the staff session after applying the phase 3 migration/permission grants. Open Reports \u8594? Finance and choose Party Outstanding. Select the branch and an as-on date, then Run report. Filters are submitted together; changing them displays a reminder and disables output until rerun. Verify the totals cover all pages.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Use the phase 2 fixture before FIFO: invoice outstanding 7,000; available credits 4,000; net outstanding 3,000. Party Outstanding should show debits 7,000, credits 4,000 and net 3,000. After the remaining 4,000 is matched, debits 3,000 and credits 0 leave the same net.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. Customer \u8594? Account \u8594? View ledger preselects that customer and branch. Choose a date range spanning its opening credit, invoice and receipt. Expect opening before the from-date, dated debit/credit entries, neutral match rows, running balance and closing 3,000. Closing must equal Party Outstanding for the same branch/party/to-date. Move the from-date forward and verify the preceding transactions become opening rather than disappearing from the balance.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. Run Age-wise Outstanding using 5/10/15/20/25 limits. Every debit belongs to exactly one of six bands based on its Lagos calendar bill date; sum the bands and compare with outstanding debits. Credits are separate and deducted to reach net. Reject duplicate/decreasing/zero/fractional limits. Admin \u8594? Settings \u8594? Party reports can save defaults; reopening the report should use them unless the run overrides them.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 5. Run Bill-wise Outstanding. Expect each open invoice/debit note/opening debit, then unadjusted receipts/credit notes/opening credits and party net. Fully matched documents are absent. Create an advance-only test party: age/bill must hide its net credit by default and show it when Show customers with a credit balance is enabled. Party Outstanding includes credit balances.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 6. On customer create/edit, choose Dealer or FA party independently of individual/company type. Test the report party-status filter. Select From party and To party using their code/name search grid; check inclusive ranges and name/code ordering. Changing order/branch clears the range. Creditors remain hidden.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 7. Save reports for a past date, perform a later-dated adjustment/reversal/receipt edit/cancellation, then rerun the earlier date. Earlier monetary results must stay the same. Current ledger shows the later reversal/edit/cancellation. An attempt to spend restored credit using a date before the recorded reversal must fail. Intentional new backdated documents can restate prior dates.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 8. Choose Print all results; allow the report window, inspect print preview, and confirm ledger/bill starts each party on a new page. Output includes all matching pages, even when the screen is on a later page. Verify opening/closing/net and printed dates. Calendar dates use Africa/Lagos.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 9. Choose Export Excel, save the .xml workbook and open it in Excel. Check all rows, numeric currency cells, totals, custom age labels, date display, punctuation in names/narrations and long text. A name beginning with = must remain text. Save As .xlsx if desired. Browser disk streaming handles large exports; browsers without that support reject output above the 20 MB fallback cap and prompt for narrower filters.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 10. Test Accountant/BillingOfficer own-branch reports and Admin all/selected-branch reports. Direct foreign-branch calls and missing report permissions must fail on JSON, print and export. Only Admin/SuperAdmin can change ageing defaults. Check loading, empty, error/retry states and phone-width scrolling. PostgreSQL-backed report, historical edit/cancellation, cursor and migration checks passed on an isolated disposable database. Browser, Excel and print-preview checks remain pending; automated tests do not substitute for these steps.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Phase 4 debit credit notes registers and Tally\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Use an isolated test database with migrations applied and a refreshed staff session. These are manual frontend acceptance steps; automated PostgreSQL evidence is recorded in the progress log.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. Sign in as Accountant or Admin. Select a branch in the app header, then Finance \u8594? Receipts \u8594? Debit Note. Choose New debit note. Select a customer by name or code and confirm the customer code and address are read-only. Enter today's Lagos date and a required narration.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Test a plain debit: choose Amount, enter 500.00 and save. Expect a generated YYYY###### number, Active status and outstanding 500.00. Open its details and Print note. Inspect the number/date, party/address, narration, branch, status, total and remaining amount.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. For the receipt flow, prepare a separate customer with a 10,000 invoice fully paid by a 10,000 receipt. Its invoice outstanding is 0. Choose a Receipt debit note for that customer. Search the receipt number or cheque number and enter 6,000 against it. The footer becomes 6,000; selecting multiple receipts sums the debit automatically. Changing receipt pages must preserve selected amounts.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. Save the receipt debit and verify the original receipt and paid invoice stay unchanged. Customer Account and Party Outstanding show a new outstanding debit of 6,000. Bill-wise lists the debit note; Age-wise places it according to its note date. Active receipts remain selectable when fully adjusted or already Tally-posted.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 5. Check invalid input: receipt debit above 10,000, negative/zero/fractional-penny amounts, empty narration, future date, no receipt lines and a receipt dated after the note day. The form or server must reject them. Receipts from another party/branch and inactive accounts must also be rejected server-side.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 6. Finance \u8594? Receipts \u8594? Credit Note \u8594? New credit note. Select the same customer. Enter credit amount 2,000 and account lines 1,200 plus 800 using active Tally accounts by code/name. Enter line narrations. Confirm the footer shows lines 2,000 and difference 0. Changing the lines to 1,900 disables Save and shows the 100 difference. Enter in a line amount adds another line; remove it if unused. Save with a required header narration.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 7. Customer Account now shows available credit 2,000 and net outstanding 4,000 against the receipt debit. The credit note appears in the adjustment credit grid. If a later invoice of 5,000 is added, total debit outstanding is 11,000, credits 2,000 and net 9,000.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 8. Apply the credit note's 2,000 to that later invoice through Advance Adjustment. Invoice outstanding becomes 3,000 and credit note unadjusted becomes 0. Net remains 9,000. The note and report screens should refresh after the mutation. Cancellation must fail while an active adjustment remains.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 9. For an unposted note only, Admin may reverse an eligible adjustment. Once the credit note's full 2,000 is restored, open it and choose Cancel note. A remark is required, with Keep note / Confirm cancellation actions. After confirmation it remains visible as Cancelled, unadjusted is 0, available credit falls by 2,000 and the cancellation appears in the ledger. A saved report for a date before cancellation keeps its earlier balance.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 10. Reports \u8594? Finance \u8594? Debit Note Register and Credit Note Register. Select From/To dates and current/all branches (Admin). Run the report. Confirm columns include receipt references or account splits, saved code/name, narration, amount, outstanding/unadjusted, status and Tally voucher. Compare all-page totals with the fixture. Cancelled face amounts remain in amount totals and contribute zero remaining balance. Opening notes are absent.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 11. Print all results and Export Excel. Allow the print window and inspect repeated headings, all rows and totals. Open the .xml workbook in Excel; verify numeric amounts, saved text, escaped punctuation and a name/narration beginning with = staying text. Export must include all matching rows rather than only the current screen page.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 12. In Tally, import active party/accounts through the existing ledger flow and map the customer to its party ledger. Under Account mappings choose Debit Note and configure both RECEIPT and AMOUNT account roles. Credit notes use their saved account lines directly.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 13. Choose the note date and Debit notes / Credit notes in the Tally document selector. Export selected XML and inspect Debit Note / Credit Note voucher types, date/number, balanced party/account signs and bill references. A missing debit mapping or inactive credit account must be skipped with a clear reason. Export is pending; resume the batch rather than exporting a duplicate.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 14. Import into a disposable Tally company, then enter the returned voucher reference and Record confirmed postings. Verify the note register/details show the reference. Posted notes cannot be cancelled. If a posted credit is subsequently adjusted, reversing that batch must fail. Opening balances never appear in Tally note selection, and adjustments generate no journal.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 15. If an unposted exported note is cancelled before external import, its pending XML must disappear and confirmation of the old batch must fail. Do not import the old downloaded XML. If XML was already imported externally, confirm the posting first; the app cannot discover that external state automatically.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 16. Test permissions: Accountant can create/read/cancel eligible notes and use registers; BillingOfficer has no note grants by default. Removing only debit read must hide debit documents and their pending XML while leaving permitted credit access intact. Register access does not grant cancellation. Direct JSON/print/export/create/cancel calls from a foreign or missing branch must fail. Admin can read selected/all branches and creates notes for parties in the selected branch.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 17. Check loading skeletons, empty results, failed lookup/report Retry actions, phone-width horizontal table scrolling, keyboard party/account search, and disabled Save while submitting. Retrying identical create details must return the same note number, with no duplicate wallet credit.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Capture before/after invoice, receipt, wallet and report totals; note numbers/status; print previews; workbook cells; Tally skip/confirm results; and permission failures. Browser, Excel, print preview and external Tally-company execution remain pending.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Phase 5 outstanding repair credit terms and letters\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s3\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\fs24 Credit terms and overdue bills\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. Sign in as Admin and open Finance \u8594? Receipts \u8594? Outstanding Letters or Update Outstanding. In Credit terms and letter settings, save company default credit days \b 30\b0 . Keep letter prefix \b DML\b0 .\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Open a test customer's edit form. Leave Credit days blank and save. Complete a billable job and create its job bill from Finance. On the invoice list verify the due date is the bill's Lagos calendar date plus 30 days.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. Set another customer's Credit days to \b 0\b0 , create a new job bill, and verify its due date is today. It remains Unpaid or Partially Paid throughout the due date. Changing customer terms or the company default affects future bills, not previously saved due dates.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. For an unposted unpaid test invoice, use its existing Edit action to set Due date to yesterday. Refresh the invoice list; it should show \b Overdue\b0 . Receive a partial payment or apply a credit, then refresh: it should stay Overdue while any amount remains. Pay the remaining amount: status becomes Paid.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 5. Open the dashboard/finance overview and check its overdue count against the unpaid past-due bills. The server performs an overdue sweep on startup and checks for a new Lagos day hourly. If the server was stopped at midnight, the startup sweep catches up. Existing invoices with no due date are preserved; edit the due date explicitly when appropriate.\par
\pard\s3\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\fs24 Preview and apply an outstanding repair\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. As Admin, select the intended branch, then Finance \u8594? Receipts \u8594? Update Outstanding. Choose Name wise or Code wise, optionally Party status, From party and To party. Ranges are inclusive. All branches is available to Admin/SuperAdmin.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Click \b Preview differences\b0 . A healthy account should show checked document count and zero differences. Review any document's old/new balance and status, and the separate customer available-credit cache table. The customer credit cache is global; the document repair respects the selected branch.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. Click \b Apply reviewed differences\b0  only after reviewing the preview. Expect a success message, updated amounts/statuses and an audit event for every changed document/cache. Preview again: no differences should remain.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. For a controlled repair test, ask the developer to corrupt a cached balance in the disposable database, without changing its face amount or allocations. For example, a 10,000 invoice with active allocations of 3,000 should recalculate to \b 7,000\b0 , regardless of an incorrect stored 6,000. A receipt of 5,000 with allocations of 3,000 should have an advance of \b 2,000\b0 . Never simulate this by changing production financial data.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 5. Preview, then use another session to make a real payment against that party. Applying the older preview must fail with \b Balances changed after preview\b0 . Run a new preview and review it again.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 6. Invalid active allocations, overallocated documents, and cancelled documents with active allocations are rejected for reconciliation; the repair does not hide them by forcing a zero balance. For a large selection, narrow the party range: each preview supports at most \b 2,000 documents and 2,000 parties\b0 .\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 7. Accountant and BillingOfficer must have no Update Outstanding action or direct access. Custom roles need both an Admin/SuperAdmin role and outstanding:recalculate. Repair changes cached balances and statuses; original amounts, allocations, dates and Tally vouchers stay as recorded.\par
\pard\s3\keepn\sb220\sa100\b\fs24 Generate and print outstanding letters\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 1. Use the Phase 2 account state with net outstanding \b 3,000\b0 , or a separate known fixture. Open Finance \u8594? Receipts \u8594? Outstanding Letters.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 2. Choose today's As on date, Name wise/Code wise, Customer/Dealer or both, and an optional From/To party range. Use threshold \b 3,000\b0  and click \b Preview parties\b0 . The party with net exactly 3,000 must be excluded.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 3. Change the threshold to \b 2,999.99\b0  and preview again. That party must appear with net 3,000. FA parties are excluded. Credits reduce net outstanding; a credit-only or zero-net party is excluded at threshold 0.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 4. Click \b Generate saved letters\b0 . Expect one reference per selected party, such as DML000001. Record the actual references. Each run supports at most \b 100 parties and 10,000 open document rows\b0 ; narrow ranges for larger runs.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 5. Select the generated letters and click \b Print selected letters\b0 . Allow the print window. Check the saved company/branch letterhead, reference, generation date, As on date, name/address, net outstanding and bill table. The table shows open debits and available credits so the net amount can be reconciled. Each party starts on a new page; long tables continue with repeated headers.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 6. If the print dialog is cancelled, do not confirm. After successful printing or saving to PDF, click \b Confirm printed successfully\b0 . Expect Printed = Yes in saved letters. The app records printing, not email/post delivery.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 7. Preview the same filters with Include parties with previously printed letters off. The printed party must be absent. Enable it and preview: the party reappears if still over the threshold. Print exclusion applies within the selected branch; All branches considers any printed letter for the party.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 8. In Saved letters and reprints enter From reference and To reference, then \b Find saved letters\b0 . Select the earlier letter and print it again. The saved name, address, table, amounts and content must stay identical even after later payments, customer edits or template changes. A repeated print confirmation preserves the first printed timestamp.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 9. Test a future As on date, negative/non-numeric threshold, inverted reference range and a foreign-branch letter. Expect validation/access errors without creating or exposing letters. After a network error, retry Generate with the same filters before starting another preview. That retry returns the original letters, not new references. After reloading the page, check saved letters first.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 10. As Admin, edit Letter content using all five placeholders: \f1 \{\{customerName\}\}\f0 , \f1 \{\{address\}\}\f0 , \f1 \{\{asOn\}\}\f0 , \f1 \{\{totalOutstanding\}\}\f0 , \f1 \{\{billTable\}\}\f0 . Save settings and generate a new preview/letter. The changed content affects new letters only. Unknown/missing placeholders are rejected; typed HTML is treated as text.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 11. Change the prefix to a separate test series such as DMT, save and generate a new letter. It should use DMT with six digits. Restore DML afterwards. References continue their own sequence when a previous prefix is restored.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 12. Test Accountant/BillingOfficer letters within their assigned branch, and Admin selected/all branches. Removing letter:outstanding must hide and reject generation, lookup, print and print confirmation. Only Admin/SuperAdmin can save company settings.\par
\pard\s2\keepn\sb260\sa140\b\fs29 Record the acceptance results\b0\fs22\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 For each scenario record tester, date, role, branch, customer code, document/reference numbers, expected result, actual result and Pass/Fail. Attach before/after screenshots, print previews, workbook results and Tally test-company voucher references where relevant. Record any failure with exact reproduction steps and the visible error text.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 Recommended execution order: customer setup \u8594? opening/advance \u8594? manual adjustment \u8594? FIFO/reversal \u8594? credit application \u8594? notes \u8594? reports \u8594? Tally \u8594? overdue \u8594? repair \u8594? letters \u8594? role/branch/mobile checks. Use separate fixtures for destructive cancellation/reversal checks so the main numeric examples remain reproducible.\par
\pard\s0\sl276\slmult1\sa120 The automated suite verifies financial and database behavior. Browser navigation, print layout, Excel opening and actual Tally import need the manual steps above; these are not implied to have been executed by automated tests.\par
}